    "source_sha256": "cb5dbd94b8eb6257ccb8d62b98f97277a29902a4be431ccdd1c932b0d34b6756",
    "note": "WS-8 (2026-08-30): CKM_AES_CCM did not exist in this engine at all before this session. Real, non-trivial addition: OpenSSL EVP CCM requires the total plaintext length declared via a NULL-output Update call before AAD or real data (RFC 3610/SP800-38C bakes length into the first CBC-MAC block), and the tag-length ctrl must be set BEFORE the key+IV init call (confirmed empirically -- the same ctrl called after key+IV init silently produces a wrong tag). Root-caused and verified against these real ACVP vectors via standalone C programs linked directly against libcrypto (ccm_test.c / ccm_dec_test.c / ccm_dec_test2.c / ccm_zero_test.c) before touching the engine, matching the same methodology used for the SP800-108 fixes. Cases: 1 encrypt + 1 decrypt KAT per key size (128/192/256, no AAD, genuinely non-zero payload -- the naive first-match picked payloadLen=0 trivial cases initially, re-selected for real payload), 1 decrypt KAT with AAD (a payloadLen=0, AAD-only case -- CCM used GMAC-style; kept deliberately as that specific, real edge case, not swapped for a \"nicer\" one), and 1 decrypt case with a deliberately-tampered tag (testPassed=false) to confirm this engine correctly rejects it, not just that it accepts good tags."
  },
